diagnosis_text:
Affected component: L3 interconnect addressing between router2 and router3 (link_r2_r3), not router0’s RIP or egress.

Mechanism: Location A hosts (172.16.10.0/24) forward to router0 (172.16.10.1). Router0’s RIP is running and its WAN egress is up (eth2 10.16.1.1/24), with routes to remote nets via 10.16.1.2. However, traffic toward Location C must traverse router1 → router2 → router3. Both router2 and router3 have eth4 configured with the same IP 192.168.100.2/24. Because router2’s next-hop to 172.18.50/24 and 172.18.51/24 is 192.168.100.2 on eth4, this duplicate causes ARP/neighbor resolution to self, so packets are never forwarded across the r2–r3 link, yielding timeouts from Location A to Location C.

